    <!-- Agents -->
    <section class="agents" id="agents">
        <div class="agents-grid-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label label-accent">How we build agents · 2026</p>
                <h2>Agents, <em>engineered.</em></h2>
                <p class="section-lede">Most AI agents fail in production for the same four reasons. These are the patterns we design with to prevent them — drawn from <a href="https://kodama.house" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kodama</a>, a real-time voice agent we build at Ænima Labs.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="fixes">
                <article class="fix reveal">
                    <p class="fix-fail"><span>01</span>They make people wait.</p>
                    <div class="fix-visual v-speed" aria-hidden="true">
                        <span class="v-row"><em>talks</em><span class="v-lane"><i></i></span></span>
                        <span class="v-row"><em>thinks</em><span class="v-lane v-lane-slow"><i></i></span></span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Answer now, think in the background.</h3>
                    <p>The part that talks never waits for the part that thinks. Slower work — recalling, checking, planning — runs alongside and hands over notes when they are ready.</p>
                    <p class="fix-result">Replies at the speed of conversation, even by voice.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="fix reveal">
                    <p class="fix-fail"><span>02</span>They forget.</p>
                    <div class="fix-visual v-budget" aria-hidden="true">
                        <span class="v-seg v-seg-rules" style="--w: 18%">rules</span>
                        <span class="v-seg" style="--w: 26%">brief</span>
                        <span class="v-seg" style="--w: 30%">recent</span>
                        <span class="v-seg v-seg-recall" style="--w: 26%">recalled</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Rebuild what it knows, every turn.</h3>
                    <p>Before each reply, the agent gathers exactly what it needs within a fixed budget — and room for the safety rules is always kept. Long-term memory has a single, careful writer, and every entry keeps its source.</p>
                    <p class="fix-result">Consistent behaviour across hour-long sessions.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="fix reveal">
                    <p class="fix-fail"><span>03</span>They make things up.</p>
                    <div class="fix-visual v-cite" aria-hidden="true">
                        <span class="v-claim"><b></b><b></b></span><span class="v-pill">source&nbsp;✓</span>
                        <span class="v-claim v-claim-short"><b></b></span><span class="v-pill v-pill-none">“I don't know”</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Cite a source, or say so.</h3>
                    <p>Answers about your business come from your own documents, found by searching for both words and meaning. Every claim points to where it came from; when nothing does, the agent says it doesn't know.</p>
                    <p class="fix-result">Answers your team can check — and trust.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="fix reveal">
                    <p class="fix-fail"><span>04</span>Nobody can tell why.</p>
                    <div class="fix-visual v-evals" aria-hidden="true">
                        <span class="v-bars"><i class="v-low" style="--h: 34%"></i><i class="v-low" style="--h: 48%"></i><i class="v-low" style="--h: 42%"></i><i class="v-low" style="--h: 60%"></i><i style="--h: 74%"></i><i style="--h: 82%"></i><i style="--h: 88%"></i><i style="--h: 96%"></i></span>
                        <span class="v-pass">ship ✓</span>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Test before shipping. Record every turn.</h3>
                    <p>Every model or prompt change is scored against a set of real cases before it goes live. Prompts are versioned, and each turn records what it used — so any answer can be traced back.</p>
                    <p class="fix-result">Changing a model is a measured decision, not a gamble.</p>
                </article>
            </div>

            <div class="agents-foot reveal">
                <div>
                    <p class="stack-label">Tools we reach for</p>
                    <ul class="stack" aria-label="Tools we reach for">
                        <li>Go · ADK</li><li>LiveKit · WebRTC</li><li>Whisper · Piper</li><li>SQLite FTS5 · embeddings</li><li>Postgres</li><li>Cloud Run</li><li>Ollama on Apple Silicon</li><li>Anthropic · OpenAI · Gemma</li>
