    <!-- Principles -->
    <section class="principles" id="principles">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label">Guiding principles</p>
                <h2>How we work.</h2>
                <p class="section-lede">Excellence in AI and engineering requires more than technical skills. These principles guide how we work and deliver exceptional results.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="principle-grid">
                <article class="principle reveal">
                    <h3>Be cool</h3>
                    <p>Exceptional people are neither ordinary nor dull. They strive to find a niche for their unique abilities and work to inspire others.</p>
                    <blockquote>“If you've gotta think about being cool, you ain't cool.”<cite>Keith Richards</cite></blockquote>
                </article>
                <article class="principle reveal">
                    <h3>Move fast</h3>
                    <p>Exceptional people focus on progressing towards set business goals in small iterations. This allows them to be flexible and change direction where needed while keeping a sporty, enduring pace.</p>
                    <blockquote>“The first principle is that you must not fool yourself — and you are the easiest person to fool.”<cite>Richard Feynman</cite></blockquote>
                </article>
                <article class="principle reveal">
                    <h3>Balance</h3>
                    <p>Exceptional people know that almost every hard decision is an act of balance. That's why we ride the wave.</p>
                    <blockquote>“Life is like riding a bicycle. To keep your balance, you must keep moving.”<cite>Albert Einstein</cite></blockquote>
                </article>
                <article class="principle reveal">
                    <h3>Elevate quality</h3>
                    <p>Exceptional people have very high standards. They shape high-quality products, services and processes with exceptional, often unexpected quality.</p>
                    <blockquote>“My tastes are simple: I am easily satisfied with the best.”<cite>Sir Winston S. Churchill</cite></blockquote>
                </article>
                <article class="principle reveal">
                    <h3>Always learn</h3>
                    <p>Exceptional people are never done learning and always seek self-improvement.</p>
                    <blockquote>“There is only one good — knowledge, and one evil — ignorance.”<cite>Socrates</cite></blockquote>
                </article>
                <article class="principle reveal">
                    <h3>Build trust</h3>
                    <p>Exceptional people are honest with themselves and others. They value the strength of people's relationships over robustness of systems. They try to be helpful, instead of trying to be right.</p>
                    <blockquote>“People don't care how much you know until they know how much you care.”<cite>John C. Maxwell</cite></blockquote>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

